# Routing rules for the static-site (certified-assets) canister that hosts
# MULTI/DEX — copied into dist/ by Vite (publicDir), read there by the recipe's
# sync plugin at `icp deploy`, never served. Netlify `_redirects` syntax:
# `from  to  status`, one rule per line, first match wins — and a REAL FILE
# always wins before any rule (resolution: exact file, then the canister's own
# clean-URL rules, then these rules in order, then the 404 fallback).
#
# SPA fallback (task 1793503326). MULTI/DEX routes under `#` (hash routes), so
# `/` is the only document path the app links itself — but a path typed, pasted
# or bookmarked from an older build must still get the shell, exactly as the
# legacy asset canister's built-in index.html fallback served it. `200` makes
# this a REWRITE (the shell's bytes at the requested URL, no visible redirect);
# declaring `/*` also replaces the canister's built-in 404 page with the shell,
# so a typo'd /assets/… name answers with HTML — the same as before the switch.
/*  /index.html  200
